    "title": "Clarinda council hears calls to tighten fireworks ordinance - NewsBreak",
    "text": "kmaland.com\nwebsite\nClarinda\nClarinda council hears calls to tighten fireworks ordinance\nBy Ethan Hewett,\n3 hours ago(Clarinda) -- Clarinda officials heard calls to reduce the amount of time that fireworks can legally be shot off within city limits around the Independence Day holiday. Meeting in regular session Wednesday evening, the Clarinda City Council heard from multiple residents regarding the city's fireworks ordinance. Currently in Clarinda, residents are allowed to shoot off fireworks from June 29th through July 8th from 9 a.m. to 10 p.m. and until 11 p.m. on July 4th. Ayn Taylor was among the Clarinda residents calling for a shorter time frame and expressing concerns over how the extended period of fireworks impacts people's pets, along with veterans with post traumatic stress disorder or night workers who sleep during the day.",
